    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Property Team Paul Reddy is delighted to bring to the market this three-bedroom terrace family home, ideally positioned within a mature and highly sought-after residential setting in Malahide. Extending to approximately 80 sq. m., the property offers generous, well-proportioned accommodation throughout, together with a sunny, south-west-facing private rear garden, a small pedestrian lane at the back and excellent potential for modernisation and extension, subject to the necessary planning permission. The property benefits from gas-fired central heating and double-glazed PVC windows.\r\n\r\nThis property presents an excellent opportunity for purchasers seeking a well-located Malahide home with superb potential. While the property would benefit from some modernisation, it offers a generous layout, excellent internal space and a mature residential setting, providing the ideal opportunity for the new owner to create a home tailored to their own taste and requirements.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation is well laid out and practical, comprising a welcoming entrance hallway, a comfortable living room with fireplace and a kitchen/dining room positioned to the rear of the property. Upstairs, there are three bedrooms, comprising two generous double bedrooms and one single bedroom, together with a family bathroom. To the front, the property benefits from a private driveway providing off-street parking.\r\n\r\nTo the rear is a particularly attractive south-west-facing private garden, enjoying excellent natural light and sunshine throughout the day. The garden is mainly laid in lawn and further benefits from two concrete sheds, one of which is fully plumbed and wired and is currently utilised as a convenient laundry room, providing valuable additional storage and utility space. The rear garden also benefits from access to a small pedestrian lane at the back, providing additional convenience.\r\n\r\nThe location is superb. Inbhir Ide is a mature and well-established residential area within easy reach of Malahide Village and Malahide Castle and Demesne, with a wide selection of local schools, shops, cafés, restaurants and recreational amenities close by. The area also benefits from excellent transport links, with Dublin Airport, the M1, M50, Portmarnock and Swords all easily accessible.\r\n\r\nThis is a fantastic opportunity to acquire a three-bedroom terrace family home in a highly desirable Malahide location, offering generous accommodation, a sunny south-west-facing private rear garden, private off-street parking and excellent potential for modernisation and extension, subject to planning permission."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "GROUND FLOOR: \r\nPorch                                 1.74 x 0.83m\r\nHall\t                              3.73 x 1.74m     Tiled flooring \r\nLiving Room                     4.39 x 3.45m      Carpeted flooring, featuring a fireplace.\r\nKitchen/Dining                5.28 x 2.83m      Open-plan kitchen/dining. Fully fitted units, tiled splashback, tiled flooring.\r\n\r\nFIRST FLOOR: \r\n\r\nLanding              2.43 x 1.73m \t  Carpeted flooring \r\nBedroom 1        4.39 x 3.05m   Carpeted flooring, built-in wardrobes\r\nBedroom 2        3.45 x 2.83m \t  Carpeted flooring, built-in wardrobe\r\nBedroom 3        3.13 x 2.12m   Carpeted flooring, built-in wardrobe\r\nBathroom          1.74 x 1.54m   Shower, WHB, WC, fully tiled."
